{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>As I commanded.</b> Meaning — regarding the eating, He had already commanded that they should eat it, and now He commands regarding the place. From this you learn: there is a commandment regarding the eating, and a commandment regarding the place; and if he wishes not to eat, behold this nullifies the commandment, and if he wishes to eat outside the place, behold this nullifies the commandment. And His saying <b>לֵאמֹר</b> ('saying') means — not that He commanded on His own initiative, but from what was said to Him from the mouth of the Shekhinah." "<b>חסלת פרשת צו</b>\n(The portion of Tzav is concluded.)"], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:54:24.391859644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}